plugin.json version: 0.1.0  (all runs preload evals/helpers/no-network.mjs; any attempt prints NETWORK-ATTEMPT)
$ lib/verify/contact-sheet.mjs --help
contact-sheet — sample frames from a video into a labelled JPEG grid

Usage: contact-sheet [options] <video>

Each frame is stamped with its time (seconds, or m:ss.ss) in the top-left corner. Default: one frame every 0.5 s.

Options:
  -o, --out <file.jpg>  Output JPEG (default: <video>.contact.jpg)
      --every <time>    Sample interval, e.g. 0.5s or 250ms (default: 0.5s)
      --count           Sample n evenly spaced frames instead
      --at <t,t,...>    Sample exactly these times (e.g. 0.5s,1.2s or ms values)
      --cols            Frames per row (default: 4)
      --width           Width of each frame (default: 480)
      --json            Print the sampled times as JSON
  -h, --help            Show this help and exit
      --version         Print the plugin version and exit

Examples:
  contact-sheet out/final.mp4 --every 0.5s -o review/contact-final.jpg
  contact-sheet renders/plates/p1.mp4 --count 8
exit=0
